WEBVTT

00:00:00.551 --> 00:00:09.954
Welcome to the Board of Studies portal of JAIN University. This walkthrough shows how a department fills its record, stage by stage.

00:00:11.082 --> 00:00:14.883
Section 1. Signing in and your home page.

00:00:16.243 --> 00:00:24.846
Open the portal and sign in with the username and password the Office of Academic Affairs issued to your department.

00:00:35.388 --> 00:00:47.597
The first time on a computer, the portal asks who you are. Your name and e-mail go with every change you save, so the Office knows who did what.

00:00:58.545 --> 00:01:05.549
Your home page shows the next step, with one button to continue where you left off.

00:01:08.147 --> 00:01:13.948
Below it, how many stages are done, and your submissions, programme by programme.

00:01:15.427 --> 00:01:26.433
The menu on the left takes you to every stage: Department Information, Pre-BoS, BoS Documents and Curriculum. A blue dot means in progress; green means submitted.

00:01:26.912 --> 00:01:29.517
Section 2. Department Information.

00:01:30.453 --> 00:01:37.856
Stage one is Department Information. Your department's name, faculty, school and campus come from the Office's records.

00:01:39.461 --> 00:01:46.466
Below, tick the programmes you run this year: UG on the left, PG on the right.

00:01:48.143 --> 00:01:55.548
A programme missing from the list? Add it here. Remove takes off one you do not run.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:02:05.291
There is no save button. Every change saves itself, and the bar at the end of the page says so.

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:08.436
Section 3. Pre-BoS.

00:02:09.502 --> 00:02:16.902
Stage two, Pre-BoS, collects the signed DIAC and DPAC compositions and the minutes of the Pre-BoS meeting.

00:02:18.155 --> 00:02:27.954
Download the template, fill it in, sign it, and upload it: as a Word file, or as a signed PDF or scanned copy.

00:02:29.302 --> 00:02:33.904
Drag a file onto the box, or press Choose file.

00:02:37.717 --> 00:02:52.720
Each upload is read straight away. A Word form is checked row by row, and the keywords show whether it is the right document. It is only a guide: a scanned copy is fine to submit.

00:02:54.314 --> 00:03:00.916
Open or View shows the file. Remove takes it away, so you can upload another.

00:03:01.702 --> 00:03:04.304
Section 4. BoS Documents.

00:03:05.356 --> 00:03:11.960
Stage three, BoS Documents: the date of the Board of Studies meeting, and its documents.

00:03:13.581 --> 00:03:26.185
The composition of BoS members, profiles of the external experts, the minutes, geotagged photos, the attendance sheet, the vision and mission, and the stakeholder feedback, each in its own box.

00:03:27.539 --> 00:03:33.343
A red star marks a document you must upload. The others are optional.

00:03:33.862 --> 00:03:36.464
Section 5. Curriculum.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:44.603
Stage four is the Curriculum, programme by programme. Choose UG or PG, then open a programme.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:56.801
Each programme has three parts: Curriculum, Syllabus and Course Revision, for the current batch, and the same for each earlier batch.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:05.560
Programme details come first. For a UG programme, the degree is worked out from its programme structure.

00:04:06.967 --> 00:04:10.370
Write the programme's objectives, one per line.

00:04:13.114 --> 00:04:22.515
Then its Programme Outcomes and Programme Specific Outcomes. Add the next one with the button. Every course's CO-PO mapping takes these columns.

00:04:24.041 --> 00:04:31.045
The regulations follow. Where a box shows grey sample wording, leaving it empty accepts that wording.

00:04:33.226 --> 00:04:40.627
The programme structure lists every course, semester by semester, with its category, L-T-P-E hours, credits and marks.

00:04:42.222 --> 00:04:52.829
The credit tables fill themselves from the structure, and the UGC Table 2 strip at the top tells you whether the credits meet the requirement.

00:04:56.514 --> 00:04:59.115
Section 6. Syllabus.

00:05:01.146 --> 00:05:09.747
The Syllabus has one sheet per course. Pick a semester and a course. Its information comes straight from the Curriculum.

00:05:13.844 --> 00:05:19.648
The course objectives start from the programme's objectives. Change them for the course.

00:05:20.906 --> 00:05:29.110
Write each course outcome and choose its level of Bloom's Taxonomy. A level is suggested from the first word.

00:05:31.965 --> 00:05:42.569
In the CO-PO-PSO mapping, choose 1, 2 or 3 for each outcome against each PO and PSO, and type the articulation figure for each column.

00:05:43.982 --> 00:05:55.786
Then the course content, module by module, with its hours, the outcomes it serves and its Bloom's level, and then the text books, book references and web references.

00:05:57.555 --> 00:06:00.156
Section 7. Course Revision.

00:06:01.329 --> 00:06:06.331
Course Revision compares each course's previous syllabus with the revised one.

00:06:07.841 --> 00:06:13.242
The summary counts the courses and gives the average percentage of revision.

00:06:15.216 --> 00:06:21.820
Further down, each course shows its modules, previous and revised, with the percentage of change.

00:06:23.554 --> 00:06:26.155
Section 8. Earlier batches.

00:06:30.846 --> 00:06:41.851
Earlier batches are chosen at the top. Each has its own Curriculum, Syllabus and Course Revision, for the semesters the Office has set for that batch.

00:06:43.487 --> 00:06:51.690
The batch's courses are listed as in the programme structure. The arrows open a course's syllabus or its revision.

00:06:51.672 --> 00:06:54.274
Section 9. Checking and submitting.

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:04.571
Everything saves as you type. Here, the objectives have been left empty.

00:07:07.072 --> 00:07:13.674
When a stage is complete, scroll to the end of the page and press Submit.

00:07:18.693 --> 00:07:27.696
The portal checks the page first. Anything missing is listed here, and Fill them now takes you straight to the box.

00:07:42.165 --> 00:07:50.766
Fill it in, and press Submit again. Once the checks pass, the part is submitted and the next one opens.

00:08:04.122 --> 00:08:11.924
A programme's last step opens a review of the whole programme: every part, and what is in it.

00:08:14.591 --> 00:08:25.595
Tick to confirm, and submit. Submitted work goes to the Office of Academic Affairs and becomes read-only. Only the Office can send it back for correction.

00:08:32.357 --> 00:08:34.961
Section 10. Reports.

00:08:38.088 --> 00:08:42.289
Reports lists every programme, with what you have submitted.

00:08:47.068 --> 00:09:00.474
See your submission shows each Curriculum, Syllabus and Course Revision exactly as the Office's Word templates lay them out. It is view only. For a copy, contact the Office of Academic Affairs.

00:09:06.676 --> 00:09:10.078
Section 11. Version history, password and help.

00:09:13.204 --> 00:09:25.006
Version History shows every saved version, who made it and when. A version can be restored as a draft, as long as that part is not yet submitted.

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:32.582
Change Password sets a new password for your department's login.

00:09:35.636 --> 00:09:42.241
And Help brings you back to this video and to the user manual. Thank you.

00:09:42.754 --> 00:09:45.356
Thank you.
